instructions:
Reads the Cloudflare API through `../cloudflare-api`; CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN needs the Account → Queues: Edit scope.

Instance example:

  // packages/infra/environments/production/delivery.ts
  import { queueModule } from '../../modules/queue'
  export default queueModule.instance({
    name: 'delivery',
    config: {
      accountId: '<account id>',
      queueName: 'myproject-delivery',
      subscriptions: [{ name: 'myproject-sending', zoneId: '<zone id>', domain: 'example.com', events: ['message.delivered', 'message.bounced'] }],
    },
  })

The consuming Worker declares the queue by name in its own wrangler config (`queues.consumers: [{ queue: 'myproject-delivery' }]`) and imports this instance, so the queue exists before wrangler attaches the consumer. `destroy` removes the subscriptions this instance names and leaves the queue.
